  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "A man accelerates from rest with a constant acceleration of $0.3\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ for the first $10$ seconds of his motion. He then jogs at a constant speed for the next $20$ seconds before accelerating with a constant acceleration of $0.1\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ for another $20$ seconds. Which graph represents the described motion?",
  "worked_solution": "We start the first line from the point $(0,0),$ since the man starts from rest. Then, because the acceleration is $0.3\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ we draw a line with slope $0.3.$ \n\nHowever, because the man is only accelerating for the first $10$ seconds, we stop the line at $t=10.$ At this time, the man's speed has increased by $0.3\\cdot 10=3\\text{\u00a0m/s}.$ So, the first line segment goes from $(0,0)$ to $(10,3).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945962/assets/b458ff6f5f08f548b07923e09aacdc103c8052103736b1adc4a76de120ade097.png)\n\nThe man then travels at a constant speed for the next $20$ seconds. So, the speed remains at $3\\,\\text{m/s}$ for the next $20$ seconds, until $t=10+20=30.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945962/assets/5c6ddd0eb8c72643fa2272f10502e8428d9c30c79d0804c54cfd7347f2178bb8.png)\n\nAfter $t=30$, the man has an acceleration of $0.1\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ so the slope of the third line segment is $0.1.$ The third line segment stops after $20$ seconds. To figure out the velocity at this moment, we need to find the equation for the third line segment.\n\nSince the third line segment passes through the point $(30,3)$ and has a slope of $0.1,$ we can use point-slope form to write the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v-{v}_{1} & =m(t-{t}_{1}) \\\\ v-3 & =0.1(t-30) \\\\ v-3 & =0.1t-3 \\\\ v & =0.1t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third line segment stops when $t=30+20=50$ seconds, and the velocity at this moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =0.1t \\\\ v & =0.1(50) \\\\ v & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the third line segment stops at the point $(50,5).$ The final graph is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945962/assets/faa567428a1f0160f77881183337e55c676a61a88cf215c757a2149811934de6.png)",
